{"nextId": 1089, "pages": [{"id": "635", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791086212505, "title": "Home", "description": "", "sections": [{"id": "637", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "tabName": "Contents", "description": "", "headings": [], "formatName": "Default"}, {"id": "638", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791086202366, "tabName": "Settings", "description": "", "headings": [], "settings": true, "formatName": "Default"}]}, {"id": "640", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791446756944, "title": "Chapter 2", "description": "Yahweh's judgement rests on truth and righteousness. After the thousand years, Jesus judges the living and the dead, and the holy city, new Jerusalem, appears.", "sections": [{"id": "641", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "tabName": "Contents", "description": "", "headings": []}, {"id": "20", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791478083263, "tabName": "Romans 2:1-16", "description": "", "headings": [{"id": "648", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791479623305, "name": "1. Yahweh God is the ultimate Judge of Men", "paragraphs": [{"id": "646", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791479547552, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "647", "rowId": "646", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791492422700, "title": "What makes God’s Judgement unique?", "text": ":::p:0: It is based on truth and righteousness.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 2:2\">Rom 2:2</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 2:5\">Rom 2:5</a>\n", "width": 1366.359375, "format": "Text Left Indent", "titleFormat": "Headers"}], "formatNames": {"rowTitle": "Headers"}}, {"id": "28", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791451577730, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "29", "rowId": "28", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791493496856, "title": "When is God’s Judgement?", "text": ":::p:7: After the great tribulation, Jesus will reigned on earth for 1,000 years, He will put all enemies under His feet and destroy Death. Then the end comes when He delivers the Kingdom to God the Father.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"1Co 15:24-26\">1Co 15:24-26</a>\n\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"1Co 15:24-26\"></a>On judgement day, God will judge men by His Son, Jesus, who died, rose again and became Lord of the living and the dead.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 2:16\">Rom 2:16</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 14:9\">Rom 14:9</a>", "width": 1366.359375, "format": "Text Left Indent", "titleFormat": "Headers"}, {"id": "30", "rowId": "28", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791451577730, "title": "", "text": "\n\n", "width": 99.265625, "format": "Footnotes", "titleFormat": "Default"}], "formatNames": {"rowTitle": "Headers"}}, {"id": "31", "order": 2, "editedAt": 1791451577730, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "32", "rowId": "31", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791459110554, "title": "What happens next?", "text": "After Jesus delivers the kingdom to His Father,\nthere will be a great and high mountain, the great city, the holy Jerusalem,\nwith the glory of God.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21:2-3\">Rev 21:2-3</a>\n\nThe <b>nations</b>, of the <b>saved</b>, shall walk in its light,\nand the kings of the earth will bring their glory and honour into it.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21:24\">Rev 21:24</a>\n\n(From the beginning, God’s plan has always been to save all nations from eternal condemnation.)\n\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21\"></a>\n\nNothing shall enter the City that defiles, or causes an abomination or a lie,\nonly those whose names are written in the Lamb’s Book of Life. \n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21:27\">Rev 21:27</a>\n\nIt is only through the ‘Lamb who was slain and rose from the grave’\nthat Mankind will be given <b>eternal life</b>.\n<b>Eternal condemnation</b> awaits those who were not saved.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Jhn 3:36\">Jhn 3:36</a>\n", "width": 1366.359375, "format": "Text Left Indent", "titleFormat": "Headers"}, {"id": "33", "rowId": "31", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791451577730, "title": "", "text": "\n\n", "width": 99.265625, "format": "Footnotes", "titleFormat": "Default"}], "formatNames": {"rowTitle": "Headers"}}], "formatName": "Default"}, {"id": "43", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791478124775, "name": "2. Man’s Judgement", "paragraphs": [{"id": "34", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791478276528, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "35", "rowId": "34", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791494142896, "title": "Who did Paul accuse of Judging without Excuse?", "text": ":::p:0: Continuing from the last verse in chapter 1 it is those who:\n\n:::p:0: • know the righteous judgement of God\n\n:::p:0: • practise things deserving of death\n\n:::p:0: • approve of some who do the same\n\n:::p:0: • yet judge others who practise such things\n\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 1:32\">Rom 1:32</a>\n\n:::p:0: <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 1:32\"></a>This description fits some scribes and Pharisees whom Jesus judged and some like them may have been in Rome:\n\n:::p:0: • Sitting in Moses’ seat but do not do what they teach <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Mat 23:2-3\">Mat 23:2-3</a>\n\n:::p:0: • Laying heavy burdens on others which they do not carry themselves <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Mat 23:4\">Mat 23:4</a>\n\n:::p:0: • Neglecting Justice Mercy and Faith <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Mat 23:23\">Mat 23:23</a>\n\n:::p:0: • Full of extortion and self-indulgence <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Mat 23:25\">Mat 23:25</a>\n\n:::p:7: • Serpents, brood of vipers, destined for hell <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Mat 23:33\">Mat 23:33</a>\n\n:::p:7: Today, this might apply to some religious leaders, politicians, business corporations, mainstream media, internet influencers and fake news.\n\nThey deceive, mislead, are hypocrites, take advantage of others and lead them away from God’s righteous ways.\n\n:::p:0: Paul told Timothy that “All Scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for:\n\n:::p:0: • doctrine,\n\n:::p:0: • <b>reproof</b>, (the exposure of error)\n\n:::p:0: • <b>correction</b>, (restoring a believer to right standing again)\n\n:::p:7: • <b>instruction</b> in righteousness\n\n:::p:0: The purpose is:\n\n\t:::p:0: <i><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 66, 170);\">“that the<b> <u>man of God</u> may be complete,\nthoroughly equipped </b>for every good work.”</span></i>\n\n\t<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"2Ti 3:16-17\">2Ti 3:16-17</a>\n\nYou may notice that ‘<b>reproof</b>’ and ‘<b>correction</b>’ actually need some form of judging behaviour.  So how do we reconcile that with:\n\n\t<span style=\"color:rgb(0, 66, 170);\"><i>“Why do you judge your brother?</i>\n<i>Or why do you show </i><i><b>contempt</b></i><i> for your brother?</i>\n<i>For </i><i><b>we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ</b></i><i>.”?</i>\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 14:10\">Rom 14:10</a></span>\n", "width": 1366.359375, "format": "Text Left Indent", "titleFormat": "Headers"}, {"id": "36", "rowId": "34", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791453705916, "title": "", "text": "\n\n", "width": 99.265625, "format": "Footnotes", "titleFormat": "Default"}], "formatNames": {"rowTitle": "Headers"}}, {"id": "37", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1791454389105, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "38", "rowId": "37", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1791493757074, "title": "Judging One Another", "text": "On the day of Judgement, Jesus the Messiah will judge every human being.\n\nThis type of judgement is for God and God alone. We are not to judge if anyone is going to be saved or not.\n\nHowever, Paul also gives instructions about people’s behaviour and the appropriate procedures, motivations and actions.\n\n\t:::p:3: <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"1Ti 5:19-20\">1Ti 5:19-20</a>\n\n\t:::p:3: <i><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 66, 170);\">19 Do not entertain an <b>accusation</b> against an elder\nunless it is brought by two or three <b>witnesses</b>.</span></i>\n\n\t:::p:7: <i><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 66, 170);\">20 But those elders who are <b>sinning</b> you are to <b>reprove before everyone</b>,\nso that the <b>others may take warning</b>.</span></i>\n\n:::p:3: In the presence of God and of Christ Jesus,\n<b>who will judge the living and the dead</b>,\nand in view of his appearing and his kingdom,\n\n:::p:3: <b>I give you this charge</b>:\n\n\t:::p:0: <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"2Ti 4:2-3\">2Ti 4:2-3</a><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"2Ti 4:2-3\"></a>\n<i><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 66, 170);\">2 <b>Preach the word</b>; be prepared in season and out of season;\n<b>correct, rebuke and encourage </b></span></i>\n\n\t:::p:3: <b><i><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 66, 170);\">— with great patience and careful instruction.</span></i></b>\n\n\t<i><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 66, 170);\">3 For the time will come <b>when people will not put up with sound doctrine.</b>\nInstead, to suit their own desires,\nthey will gather around them a great number of teachers\nto say what their itching ears want to hear.</span></i>\n\nThis is not the place to teach about judging sin in others.\nThere is plenty of teaching in the Torah and the New Testament if you follow Paul’s charge.\n\n‘Preach the <b>Word</b> of God and <b>be ready to correct and rebuke.</b>'\n\n<b>But</b> remember, only do it to encourage with love in your heart.\nCheck that there is no Judgement in your thoughts before opening your mouth;\nit may not be appropriate for you to speak or the right moment for them to hear.\n", "width": 1366.359375, "format": "Text Left Indent", "titleFormat": "Headers"}], "formatNames": {"rowTitle": "Headers"}}]}]}, {"id": "643", "order": 2, "editedAt": 1791086990990, "tabName": "Settings", "description": "", "headings": [], "settings": true}]}, {"id": "1040", "order": 2, "editedAt": 0, "title": "Chapter 4", "description": "", "sections": [{"id": "1041", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "tabName": "Contents", "description": "", "headings": []}, {"id": "1042", "order": 1, "editedAt": 0, "tabName": "God Promised", "description": "", "headings": [{"id": "1022", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794840138475, "name": "What did God actually Promise?", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1023", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1024", "rowId": "1023", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794840926384, "title": "", "text": "In Romans, God's promises are mentioned 10 times and half of them are in Chapter 4.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 1:1-2\">Rom 1:1-2</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:13-16\">Rom 4:13-16</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:20-21\">Rom 4:20-21</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 9:4\">Rom 9:4</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 9:8-9\">Rom 9:8-9</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 15:8\">Rom 15:8</a>\n\nBefore we watch a short video with an answer, here's a simple question. Just what has God promised?", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1025", "order": 1, "editedAt": 0, "name": "The Land, Forever", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1026", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1027", "rowId": "1026", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794825570877, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/1-the-land-forever.webp\" alt=\"Gen 12:7 Gen 13:15-17 Gen 15:7 Gen 15:18 Gen 17:8 Gen 26:3 Gen 28:13 Gen 35:12\" data-intext=\"White Grey left\" />Abraham link\nTime and time again, Yahweh said<span style=\"font-size:calc(18px * var(--ew-font, 1));\">, \"All the land which you see I give to you and your descendants forever.\"</span>\n\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 12:7\">Gen 12:7</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 13:15-17\">Gen 13:15-17</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 15:7\">Gen 15:7</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 15:18\">Gen 15:18</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 17:8\">Gen 17:8</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 26:3\">Gen 26:3</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 28:13\">Gen 28:13</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 35:12\">Gen 35:12</a>\n\nAfter <b>reading</b> these verses, what do you believe Yahweh meant?", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1028", "order": 2, "editedAt": 0, "name": "As the Dust and the Stars", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1029", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1030", "rowId": "1029", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794722319267, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/2-as-the-dust-and-the-stars.webp\" alt=\"\" data-intext=\"White Grey right\" />He said Abraham's children would be like the dust of the earth and the stars in the sky.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 13:16\">Gen 13:16</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 15:5\">Gen 15:5</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 22:17\">Gen 22:17</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 26:4\">Gen 26:4</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 28:14\">Gen 28:14</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:18\">Rom 4:18</a>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1031", "order": 3, "editedAt": 0, "name": "A King for the Nations", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1032", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1033", "rowId": "1032", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794825934065, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/3-a-king-for-the-nations.webp\" alt=\"He said, &quot;Kings shall come from you.&quot; Gen 17:6 Gen 17:16 Gen 35:11\" data-intext=\"White Grey left\" />He named him father of many nations.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 17:4-5\">Gen 17:4-5</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:17-18\">Rom 4:17-18</a>\n\nHe said, \"Kings shall come from you.\"\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 17:6\">Gen 17:6</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 17:16\">Gen 17:16</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 35:11\">Gen 35:11</a>\n\nAnd He said something very personal: \"I will be their God.\"\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 17:7-8\">Gen 17:7-8</a>\n\nRight at the start of Romans, the good news is about God's Son, born into David's family.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 1:1-3\">Rom 1:1-3</a>\n\nIt is for the<b> Jew first,</b> and also for the rest of the world.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 1:16\">Rom 1:16</a>\n\nGenesis had already said, \"In you all the nations shall be blessed.\"\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 12:3\">Gen 12:3</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 18:18\">Gen 18:18</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 22:18\">Gen 22:18</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 26:4\">Gen 26:4</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 28:14\">Gen 28:14</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gal 3:8\">Gal 3:8</a>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1034", "order": 4, "editedAt": 0, "name": "Heir of the World", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1035", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1036", "rowId": "1035", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794734373142, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/4-heir-of-the-world.webp\" alt=\"Then he says this is for us too. Rom 4:23-24\" data-intext=\"White Grey right\" />This week's verse goes even wider. Paul says Abraham would be \"heir of the world.\"\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:13\">Rom 4:13</a>\n\nThen he says this is for us too.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:23-24\">Rom 4:23-24</a>\n\nIf you belong to Christ, you are Abraham's family, and you share the same promise.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gal 3:29\">Gal 3:29</a>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1037", "order": 5, "editedAt": 0, "name": "Life to the Dead", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1038", "order": 0, "editedAt": 0, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1039", "rowId": "1038", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794729684795, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/5-life-to-the-dead.webp\" alt=\"Paul calls God the One who &quot;gives life to the dead.&quot; Rom 4:17-19 Heb 11:19\" data-intext=\"White Grey left\" />God also promised to deal with the things that break us. Christ came to put away sin, and He will come again.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Heb 9:26-28\">Heb 9:26-28</a>\n\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Heb 9:26-28\"></a>Paul calls God the One who \"gives life to the dead.\"\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:17-19\">Rom 4:17-19</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Heb 11:19\">Heb 11:19</a>\n\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Heb 11:19\"></a>He raised Jesus from the dead.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:24\">Rom 4:24</a>\n\nHere is the heart of it. The promise is sure, not because we are strong, but because it rests on God.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:16\">Rom 4:16</a>\n\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:16\"></a>Abraham was fully convinced that what God had promised, He was also able to do.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:21\">Rom 4:21</a>\n\nGod keeps His word. Let's see what that might look  like.", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}]}, {"id": "1066", "order": 2, "editedAt": 1794733261894, "tabName": "Promises Video", "description": "", "headings": [{"id": "1063", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794733261894, "name": "King of Kings and Lord of Lords", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1064", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794733261894, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1065", "rowId": "1064", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794733261894, "title": "", "text": "<video class=\"col-vid\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/king-of-kings-web.mp4\" data-speed=\"90\"></video>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}]}, {"id": "1067", "order": 3, "editedAt": 1794734451157, "tabName": "Fulfilled Promises", "description": "", "headings": [{"id": "1071", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794764332366, "name": "The promises, kept", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1072", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794734451157, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1073", "rowId": "1072", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794765435109, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/6-the-promises-kept.webp\" alt=\"So what brought me to this particular understanding?\" data-intext=\"White Grey left\" />The Video is my understanding of how Yahweh's promises could be fulfilled.\n\nSo what brought me to this particular understanding?\n\nYears of reading scriptures from Genesis to Revelation.", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1074", "order": 1, "editedAt": 1794764332366, "name": "Yahweh comes home", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1075", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794734451157, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1076", "rowId": "1075", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794770811863, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/7-god-comes-home.webp\" alt=\"God will live with mankind again. He will wipe away every tear. There will be no more death, and nothing less than perfection. Rev 21:3-4\" data-intext=\"White Grey right\" />In the beginning, God walked with Adam and Eve in a garden, but mankind rebelled and were expelled. Yahweh promised Abraham, \"I will be their God.\"\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 3:23-24\">Gen 3:23-24</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gen 17:7-8\">Gen 17:7-8</a>\n\nGod will live with mankind again. He will wipe away every tear. There will be no more death, and nothing less than perfection.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21:3-4\">Rev 21:3-4</a>\n\nThe earth will be made new, like that very first garden was, and this time it will last. It will be a world at peace, with the nations at rest and Yahweh at home with His children.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21:1-3\">Rev 21:1-3</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 22:1-3\">Rev 22:1-3</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Isa 2:4\">Isa 2:4</a>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1077", "order": 2, "editedAt": 1794774103204, "name": "One", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1078", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794734451157, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1079", "rowId": "1078", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794774484914, "title": "", "text": "\n\nOne man’s Promise for the whole world<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/8-one-man-the-whole-world.webp\" alt=\"\" data-intext=\"White Grey left\" />God’s promise to Abraham family is heir of His kingdom. They will inherit the whole world.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:13\">Rom 4:13</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 8:16-17\">Rom 8:16-17</a>This isn't some vague abstract mystery for theologians. A renewed earth will become Yahweh’s home for His family. And if you belong to His Son, Jesus, His home will be for you.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Gal 3:29\">Gal 3:29</a>\n", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1080", "order": 3, "editedAt": 1794764332366, "name": "Abraham waited", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1081", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794734451157, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1082", "rowId": "1081", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794841306877, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/9-abraham-waited.webp\" alt=\"We know the end from the beginning because He revealed it in the Bible. Isa 46:9-10\" data-intext=\"White Grey right\" />Some of us feel a long way from all this. Abraham did too. He waited, and he didn't see the whole promise finished in his lifetime. But he trusted the One who spoke it. \n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Heb 11:8-10\">Heb 11:8-10</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Heb 11:13\">Heb 11:13</a>\n\nWe know the end from the beginning because He revealed it in the Bible. \n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Isa 46:9-10\">Isa 46:9-10</a>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1083", "order": 4, "editedAt": 1794759928335, "name": "Why can we be sure?", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1084", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794734451157, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1085", "rowId": "1084", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794841306877, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/10-why-we-can-be-sure.webp\" alt=\"The promise doesn't depend on how strong you feel today or how good you are. It rests on God. The God who gives life to the dead. Rom 4:16-17\" data-intext=\"White Grey left\" />If your heart is weary and your thoughts are troubled, this is for you.\n\nThe promise doesn't depend on how strong you feel today or how good you are. It rests on God. The God who gives life to the dead.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:16-17\">Rom 4:16-17</a>\n\nAbraham looked at his own body, as good as dead, and he still trusted God. And God has already done the greatest by giving us His only begotten Son.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:19-21\">Rom 4:19-21</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"John 3:16\">John 3:16</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 8:32\">Rom 8:32</a>\n\nYahweh raised Jesus from the dead as proof. Proof of what?\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Acts 17:31\">Acts 17:31</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rom 4:24-25\">Rom 4:24-25</a>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}, {"id": "1086", "order": 5, "editedAt": 1794759899794, "name": "I will be his God", "formatName": "White Grey", "paragraphs": [{"id": "1087", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794734451157, "title": "", "columns": [{"id": "1088", "rowId": "1087", "order": 0, "editedAt": 1794764332366, "title": "", "text": "<img class=\"col-pic\" src=\"/sites/Romans/images/11-i-will-be-his-god.webp\" alt=\"You don't need to be an expert in the future. You do need to know the One who promised you a future. You don’t need to know when it will happen. But like Abraham, you need to know that it will happen.\" data-intext=\"White Grey right\" />The video closed with God's own words: the one who overcomes shall inherit all things. \"I will be his God, and he shall be My son.\"\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21:7\">Rev 21:7</a>\n\nYou don't need to be an expert in the future. You do need to know the One who promised you a future. You don’t need to know when it will happen. But like Abraham, you need to know that it will happen.\n\nBelieve the same God who raised Jesus, He will be back to dwell with His people who are in Christ.\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Acts 1:11\">Acts 1:11</a> <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#ref\" data-ref=\"Rev 21:3\">Rev 21:3</a>", "width": 1, "format": "White Grey", "titleFormat": "White Grey"}], "formatNames": {"paragraph": "White Grey", "rowTitle": "White Grey"}}], "borderFormat": "White Grey"}]}, {"id": "1043", "order": 4, "editedAt": 0, "tabName": "Settings", "description": "", "headings": [], "settings": true}]}]}
